The function works seamlessly across different operating systems and file systems due to the use of platform-independent functions like `os.path.getsize()`. The chunk size is optimized based on the file size and available system resources using a default value of 65536 bytes (64KB).

The function can handle files of varying sizes efficiently, from kilobytes to gigabytes, without causing excessive memory consumption or runtime errors. It provides clear and concise error messages to assist in diagnosing issues related to file integrity and hashing failures.']

