To handle memory allocation failures gracefully, the code uses std::unique_ptr, which automatically calls the deleter function when an object is destroyed or a shared_ptr's reference count reaches zero. This ensures that all allocated memory is freed when the LinkedList object is destroyed or when individual structures are no longer needed.

