The `worker()` function is designed for multithreaded access, with each worker thread modifying the shared buffer safely using a mutex. The main function creates several worker threads that append strings to the shared buffer concurrently.

To minimize lock contention and maximize throughput in a high-concurrency environment, consider using more advanced synchronization techniques like optimistic locking or lock-free data structures if performance becomes a bottleneck. Additionally, you can explore other memory management strategies like memory pools to further improve the efficiency of the buffer resizing operations.']

